course: dictionary
lesson: 5515
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word league has more than one meaning. Context, the words and sentences around it, tells you which meaning to use. «In a league a win is worth 3 points and a draw 1.» Points and wins show that league is about games, so here it is a sports competition.
explain: Look for the clues. «He is not in the same league» has no football in it. The word same tells you the sentence is about level of quality, so league means how good someone is. Ask: what meaning would fit here? Then try it in the sentence to check.
explain: Another clue is the phrase «league table». It is a list that ranks teams by points, so reading it means comparing numbers. In a story, «Twenty Thousand Leagues Under the Sea» uses an old meaning: a distance of about three miles.
fact: League has several meanings, so always check the context.
fact: A league is a group of sports teams or clubs that play matches against each other to see who is best.
fact: «He is not in the same league» means he is not at the same level of quality.
fact: A league can also be a group of people or countries who join together for a shared aim.
fact: An old league was a distance of about three miles (about 5 kilometres).
exercise: «In a league a win is worth 3 points and a draw 1.» What is a league in this sentence? | A group of people who work together in secret | A long distance of three miles | *A group of sports teams that play matches against each other | A kind of table for dinner
exercise: «He is not in the same league.» What does league mean here? | *A level of quality | A distance of three miles | A football pitch | A sports team
exercise: In «Twenty Thousand Leagues Under the Sea», what does league mean? | A level of quality | A group of countries | *A distance of about three miles | A football match
test: The countries formed a league to work together for peace. What does league mean? | A sports match | A type of table | A distance of three miles | *A group of countries joined for a shared aim
test: A football team at the top of the league table has what? | The fewest fans | The shortest name | *The most points | A pitch with no lines
exam: Which sentence uses league to mean a level of quality? | Twenty Thousand Leagues Under the Sea is a famous book | *He is not in the same league as the others | In a league a win is worth 3 points | The league table is on the wall
